r thought i'd dream  because the first super bowl  in miami i left lansing with five  white businessmen and we got to miami  and they were at the jock  i couldn't stay there i had to stay i  stayed at a black hotel  i tell you what they are well the times  certainly have changed now gregory can  stay  anywhere he wants i did ask him  christian how much he spent on this  pilgrimage to every super bowl the first  year it was a 12  ticket he would not share how much he  spent but if you add up the average  price of every super bowl ticket from 1  to 54  you would have spent over 30 thousand  dollars that does not  include travel lodging and food  so it's a really expensive hobby wow  incredible well let me ask you one more  question  now this isn't your first super bowl as  i can imagine how different is the  atmosphere  because of covert restrictions this year  well normally monday of super bowl week  is media day  and we here at some big stadium filled  with every single player every single  coach the opportunity to talk to him  but this time the chiefs won't get here  until saturday  today's virtual media day so tom brady  was sitting in a room all by himself  answering questions on zoom so yeah a  big impact covert has had  and if you think about this too  christian this  this is the first team to host the super  bowl and play it at the same time  that would be crazy but tampa bay also  had the stanley cup champion  in the tampa bay lightning they played  that in a bubble in canada  tampa bay was also in the world series  the rays they played that in a bubble in  texas  so just think about all the missed  opportunities and missed revenue for  this city  wow thank you so much jack doyle's live  from tampa thank you so much for talking  to us  well you can watch the kansas city  chiefs and the tampa bay bucks  face off in the super bowl right here on  channel 8  this sunday
 

